  "raw_receipt_sha256": "62b4ab2b3b0dcdaa55b210e5de3e8322e7e6b57201b05e085983d8ff0882afa2",
  "run_id": 44606981694,
  "schema": "component-exact-evidence-preservation-v1",
  "scope_limit": "For a rational coordinate subspace E of dimension r, let L be its actual full integer-point lattice. An integer matrix A with r columns in E and positive Gram determinant generates the sublattice M = columnSubmodule E A. Relative to an actual integer basis of L, the columns have an integer square coordinate matrix C. Lean proves that the quotient cardinality Nat.card (L \u29f8 M) equals the absolute determinant of C and is positive. It then proves the exact identity det(A\u1d40A) = [L:M]\u00b2 * covolume(L)\u00b2. The containment, dimension and positive-Gram hypotheses are explicit; no saturation or quotient-index identity is assumed.\n\nThis identifies the integer determinant factor in the earlier Gram/covolume comparison with the actual finite lattice quotient. It does not discharge the containing-plane gap or complete the six-speed classification. The six-speed result remains partial.",
  "source_commit": "a8577e5da31b851ce64333aa921b39c6623e0389"
}
